%U A399037 759627137573976006450458746,13443803434282990603390134891906,475861881162925014232657195610437408
%N A399037 Number of strongly connected digraphs on n unlabeled nodes with a distinguished node at which they are reducible as a flow graph, counted up to isomorphism fixing that node.
%C A399037 The pointed loop regions of reducible flow graphs: every reducible flow graph decomposes uniquely into such regions (its strongly connected components pointed at their headers) joined by an acyclic header-entering superstructure.
%C A399037 Equivalently: strongly connected digraphs D with a node h such that deleting the edges into h leaves a single-source flow graph rooted at h that is reducible.
%C A399037 Computed exactly by the equivariant Burnside recurrence (see _reducible_unlabeled in the linked program of A397968).
%D A399037 F. Harary and E. M. Palmer, Graphical Enumeration, Academic Press, NY, 1973.
%D A399037 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A399037 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A399037 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A399037 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%F A399037 a(n) = (1/(n-1)!) * Sum over cycle types mu of n-1 elements of permcount(mu) * F_W(mu), where F_W is the equivariant strong-region recurrence for a fixed header.
%o A399037 (Python) unlabeled_reducible_sequence("unlabeled_reducible_strong", 16) # See Python link in A397968 for program code.
%Y A399037 Cf. A397968 (assembled entry-pointed family), A035512 (all strongly connected unlabeled digraphs).
%K A399037 nonn,new
%O A399037 1,3
